{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9853f62c8f29b98b","type":"tool_result","content":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:16:Red Hat OpenShift AI (RHOAI) 3.6-ea.1 is a comprehensive AI/ML platform deployed on OpenShift Container Platform through the Operator Lifecycle Manager (OLM). The platform is orchestrated by rhods-operator, which manages the lifecycle of all platform components through a hierarchy of custom resources — DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization, and per-component CRDs. Each major capability (model serving, pipelines, distributed workloads, notebooks, model registry, training, observability, guardrails, and models-as-a-service) is implemented by a dedicated module operator or controller that watches its component CR and reconciles downstream Kubernetes resources using kustomize-based manifest rendering through the shared odh-platform-utilities framework.\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:18:The platform ingress architecture is in active transition. The rhods-operator Gateway service controller provisions a central `data-science-gateway` using Gateway API (GatewayClass, Gateway, HTTPRoutes) while maintaining backward compatibility through OpenShift Routes. kube-auth-proxy provides OIDC-authenticated access to the dashboard, and the Gateway controller conditionally integrates with Istio by dynamically creating EnvoyFilter and DestinationRule resources when Istio CRDs are detected. Models-as-a-Service introduces a parallel ingress path through Kuadrant AuthPolicy enforcement with API key, TokenReview, and optional OIDC JWT authentication at the Gateway level. Model-registry-operator implements dual ingress (Gateway API HTTPRoutes and OpenShift Routes) with kube-rbac-proxy sidecar authentication on backend pods.\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:27:rhods-operator\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:65:**rhods-operator** is the platform root: it owns all component CRDs (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI) and three service controllers (Auth, Gateway, Monitoring) that manage cross-cutting platform infrastructure. Every component operator depends on rhods-operator for activation and lifecycle management.\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:67:**kserve** is the most connected serving component with 13 CRDs, 4 independent controller binaries (manager, llmisvc, localmodel, kserve-module), and integration with Gateway API, KEDA, cert-manager, Istio, and the Gateway API Inference Extension. Both rhods-operator and model-registry depend on it.\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:79:| CRD-based orchestration | rhods-operator, kserve, odh-model-controller, models-as-a-service, kuberay, kueue-operator, trainer-operator, workbenches-operator, spark-operator, model-registry-operator, feast-module-operator, mlflow-operator, ai-gateway-operator, ogx-k8s-operator, trustyai-service-operator, data-science-pipelines-operator, mcp-lifecycle-operator, mcp-lifecycle-module-operator, llm-d-batch-gateway-operator | Each component defines cluster-scoped CRDs watched by the platform operator; component operators reconcile their own CRDs into namespace-scoped workloads |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:81:| Gateway API routing | rhods-operator, models-as-a-service, model-registry-operator, kserve (llmisvc), odh-model-controller | HTTPRoute resources reference the data-science-gateway for authenticated external access; components own their routes and bind to a shared gateway |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:82:| kube-rbac-proxy sidecar | kserve, odh-model-controller, model-registry-operator, rhods-operator (monitoring proxies), odh-dashboard | TLS-terminating authentication proxy injected as a sidecar; validates tokens via Kubernetes TokenReview/SubjectAccessReview |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:84:| Platform TLS profile alignment | rhods-operator, kserve, odh-model-controller, model-registry-operator, workbenches-operator, trainer | Operators read the OpenShift APIServer TLS security profile and apply matching cipher suites and minimum TLS version to their own endpoints |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:93:| redhat-ods-operator / opendatahub-operator-system | Operator namespace | rhods-operator |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:98:| models-as-a-service | MaaS namespace | maas-api, maas-controller; rhods-operator Auth controller watches this namespace |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:99:| kuadrant-system | Kuadrant infrastructure | Authorino/Kuadrant controllers; rhods-operator Auth controller watches this namespace |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:105:| data-science-gateway (openshift-ingress) | rhods-operator Gateway service controller | HTTPRoutes from models-as-a-service, model-registry-operator, rhods-operator, kserve llmisvc | Envoy (via Istio/SAIL or gateway-api controller) | Conditional: EnvoyFilter -> ext_authz -> kube-auth-proxy for dashboard; Kuadrant AuthPolicy for MaaS; kube-rbac-proxy sidecar for model-registry | odh-dashboard, models-as-a-service, model-registry, kserve LLMInferenceService | derived |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:106:| OpenShift Routes (various namespaces) | rhods-operator, model-registry-operator, odh-observability, trustyai-service-operator | Route resources per component | OpenShift HAProxy router | TLS termination at router; kube-rbac-proxy at pod level | odh-dashboard, model-registry REST, Prometheus proxies, TrustyAI service | observed |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:113:| data-science-gateway | openshift-ingress / platform GatewayClass | rhods-operator Gateway service controller | odh-dashboard (via kube-auth-proxy), models-as-a-service, model-registry-operator, kserve llmisvc, odh-model-controller | Per-route: EnvoyFilter ext_authz -> kube-auth-proxy (dashboard), Kuadrant AuthPolicy (MaaS), kube-rbac-proxy sidecar (model-registry) | central/shared | derived |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:118:RHOAI 3.6-ea.1 presents a multi-generation ingress architecture. The primary ingress path uses Gateway API through the `data-science-gateway`, provisioned by the rhods-operator Gateway service controller. This gateway serves as the central platform ingress node, with multiple independently owned components attaching HTTPRoutes to it. The rhods-operator creates the GatewayClass and Gateway resources, and conditionally integrates with Istio by dynamically owning EnvoyFilter and DestinationRule resources when Istio CRDs are detected on the cluster.\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:124:The EnvoyFilter -> ext_authz -> kube-auth-proxy chain for dashboard access is conditionally created by the rhods-operator Gateway controller when Istio CRDs are present. The specific filter configuration (selector, target service/port, auth-check path, route scope) is dynamically generated by the controller. Source inspection confirms that the Gateway controller owns EnvoyFilter and DestinationRule resources and deploys a kube-auth-proxy with OIDC support, but the exact ext_authz filter wiring details are rendered at reconciliation time from Go code rather than static manifests, making the full chain `derived` rather than `observed`. [source: rhods-operator internal/controller/services/gateway/gateway_controller.go:42-103]\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:141:| Istio integration | Conditional (when CRDs detected) | rhods-operator (EnvoyFilter, DestinationRule), kserve llmisvc (DestinationRule), odh-model-controller (EnvoyFilter) |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:143:| Gateway API | Primary ingress mechanism | rhods-operator, kserve, models-as-a-service, model-registry-operator, odh-model-controller, ai-gateway-operator |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:153:| kube-rbac-proxy sidecar (SubjectAccessReview) | kserve, odh-model-controller, model-registry-operator, rhods-operator (monitoring proxies), odh-dashboard, odh-observability | Pod-level TLS-terminating proxy; validates tokens via K8s TokenReview and checks authorization via SubjectAccessReview |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:155:| OAuth2/OIDC (via kube-auth-proxy) | odh-dashboard (via rhods-operator Gateway controller) | Gateway-level; kube-auth-proxy handles OAuth2 flow, session management, and token validation |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:158:| Admission webhook TLS (service-ca) | rhods-operator, kserve, odh-model-controller, models-as-a-service, workbenches-operator, odh-dashboard, kueue-operator, kuberay, spark-operator, trainer, training-operator | Webhook endpoints; TLS certificates provisioned by OpenShift service-CA operator |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-3k43c7al/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:164:| FIPS-compliant build (strictfipsruntime) | rhods-operator, kserve (kserve-module), kube-auth-proxy, models-as-a-service, odh-model-controller, odh-dashboard, model-registry-operator, ai-gateway-operator, trainer-operator, workbenches-operator, feast-module-operator, mlflow-operator, spark-operator, kueue-operator, kuberay, mcp-lifecycle-module-operator, mcp-lifecycle-operator, ogx-k8s-operator, trustyai-service-operator, data-science-pipelines-operator | CGO_ENABLED=1 + GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime routes Go crypto through system Open