{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac66e37790fdcd86","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n3\ttitle: CI lint enforcement for structured reconciliation log fields\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 0\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: 1\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 5\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# CI Lint Enforcement for Structured Reconciliation Log Fields\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic adds a CI lint/static-analysis rule to the rhods-operator repository that flags any `log.Error` call in a reconciliation error path missing the required structured fields (`name`, `namespace` for namespaced resources, `resourceKind`). It is the durable enforcement mechanism for the structured log convention: the conversion work makes existing call sites conform, and this rule keeps them conforming as new code lands. The rule is enabled in enforcing mode once both binaries' call sites conform; enabling it earlier would fail CI against the non-conforming baseline.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Implement a lint/static-analysis check (repository-appropriate mechanism: linter rule, AST-based check, or CI script) that detects `log.Error` calls in reconciliation error paths missing required structured fields or embedding resource identity in the message string.\n40\t- Wire the check into the repository's CI pipeline so it runs on every pull request.\n41\t- Enable the check in enforcing mode across both the manager and cloudmanager binaries once their call-site conversions are complete (the conversion work is tracked separately; this epic's gate goes live against the conformed codebase).\n42\t- Provide an actionable CI failure message pointing contributors to the structured log field convention.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- Given a fixture containing `log.Error` calls that embed resource identity in message text or omit required structured fields, when the lint rule runs, then every violating call is flagged, measured by the rule's test/fixtures run.\n47\t- Given the rhods-operator repository with both binaries' conversions complete, when CI runs the check in enforcing mode, then it reports zero findings across the manager and cloudmanager binaries, measured by a green CI run.\n48\t- Given a pull request introducing a new `log.Error` call missing required structured fields, when CI runs, then the check fails with a message referencing the convention, measured by a deliberate test violation on a branch.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- HLR1 (P0, supporting) — delivers the \"measured by CI lint rule or static analysis\" verification instrument for the embedded-identity conversion and the audit-completeness risk mitigation; the conversion epics verify their own completeness via static-analysis census, so this epic is an enforcement/ratchet follow-on rather than a prerequisite of the P0 conversions.\n53\t\n54\t## Risks / Notes\n55\t\n56\t- The rule's activation is gated on the conformance of both binaries (manager and cloudmanager conversion work completing first); the rule itself can be developed and tested against fixtures in parallel.\n57\t- If a repository-appropriate lint mechanism already exists, prefer extending it over adding a new tool.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c4a33f5d4febd9e","agent_id":"af261a6c2b9cc1ff0","session_id":"8da6b11c-1205-4d00-b52a-b6889016afe4","uuid":"f52e7daf-28e2-41fa-a652-bdb9e243a4e9","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:20:54.295Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac66e37790fdcd86","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
