rformed (pipeline-computed).\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\nEvery epic has testable ACs with explicit measurement instruments (static-analysis\ncensus, unit tests on test logger output, green CI run, published-content checks,\nrecorded review sign-off). Rule-mandated ACs: E004 (docs-authoring) has the technical\nreview AC (\"reviewed against the implemented logging changes... recorded review\nsign-off\"); no konflux-chain or replacement epics exist (the log change is additive per\nthe NFR, and the backwards-compatibility before/after ingestion verification AC is\npresent on both conversion epics). No misfiled soft ACs: the externally-controlled items\n(COO adoption, cloudmanager release timing) are correctly placed in Risks/Notes and\nHealth Warnings, and E004's publication AC is scoped to the epic's own deliverables\n(published convention + filed tracking issues), explicitly excluding adoption. No\ndraft-ID references to sibling epics in any epic body (only full epic IDs in frontmatter\ndependencies).\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\nEvery strategy acceptance criterion is accounted for: embedded-identity conversion\n(E001/E002), DSCI key migration + release notes with query examples (E001), service\ncontroller resourceKind (E001), action-file fields across all 15 files in 4 tiers (E001),\ncloudmanager fields (E002), cluster-scoped resource handling (E001 and E002 ACs), and\nthe contribution guideline (E004). The CI lint rule from the strategy's first AC\nmeasurement and the risk-mitigation plan is delivered by E003. Strategy-level context is\ncarried forward, not dropped: the log-consumer regression risk and SRE/Support\ncoordination are ACs/risks on E001 and E002; the missed-path risk is mitigated by the\ncensus + downstream lint; the single-release DSCI migration constraint is an E001 risk\nnote; all four open questions are explicitly dispositioned. The \"Design doc: to be\ncreated\" from Supporting Documentation is subsumed by E004's guideline scope (