ce controllers, DSCInitialization, the 15-action-file architecture, and the\n89\tcloudmanager binary (`cmd/cloudmanager`) with its AWS/Azure/CoreWeave engine controllers.\n90\tNo arithmetic or threshold checks performed (pipeline-computed).\n91\t\n92\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n93\tEvery epic has testable ACs with explicit measurement instruments (static-analysis\n94\tcensus, unit tests on test logger output, green CI run, published-content checks,\n95\trecorded review sign-off). Rule-mandated ACs: E004 (docs-authoring) has the technical\n96\treview AC (\"reviewed against the implemented logging changes... recorded review\n97\tsign-off\"); no konflux-chain or replacement epics exist (the log change is additive per\n98\tthe NFR, and the backwards-compatibility before/after ingestion verification AC is\n99\tpresent on both conversion epics). No misfiled soft ACs: the externally-controlled items\n100\t(COO adoption, cloudmanager release timing) are correctly placed in Risks/Notes and\n101\tHealth Warnings, and E004's publication AC is scoped to the epic's own deliverables\n102\t(published convention + filed tracking issues), explicitly excluding adoption. No\n103\tdraft-ID references to sibling epics in any epic body (only full epic IDs in frontmatter\n104\tdependencies).\n105\t\n106\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n107\tEvery strategy acceptance criterion is accounted for: embedded-identity conversion\n108\t(E001/E002), DSCI key migration + release notes with query examples (E001), service\n109\tcontroller resourceKind (E001), action-file fields across all 15 files in 4 tiers (E001),\n110\tcloudmanager fields (E002), cluster-scoped resource handling (E001 and E002 ACs), and\n111\tthe contribution guideline (E004). The CI lint rule from the strategy's first AC\n112\tmeasurement and the risk-mitigation plan is delivered by E003. Strategy-level context is\n113\tcarried forward, not dropped: the log-consumer regression risk and SRE/Support\n114\tcoordination are